# Tools the repo's own tooling shells out to. Every entry is justified by a real
# call site. This file is data: one tool per line, `#` comments and blank lines
# ignored, no shebang and no executable bit.
#
# .ci/check-devshell-provides reads this file in both directions:
# - forward: every entry here must resolve on PATH inside the devShell;
# - reverse: every devShell package must ship one of these binaries, OR back a
#   formatter .treefmt.nix enables.
#
# That second escape is why prettier, yamlfmt, nixfmt and taplo are absent:
# treefmt runs them from the Nix store, never through PATH, and the lint derives
# their exemption from .treefmt.nix rather than from a list kept here.

# invoked by .ci/run-lint-checks
actionlint
# run-tests invokes bats from PATH; the devShell provides it
bats
# invoked by .githooks/commit-msg
commitlint
# invoked by .ci/run-lint-checks
editorconfig-checker
# invoked by .ci/run-lint-checks
deadnix
# invoked by .ci/run-lint-checks
statix
# the hook's own runtime dependency, and scanner.bats drives it directly
gawk
# one-true-awk (BWK); run-tests --awk=bwk shims `awk` to it
nawk
# asserted by .ci/check-uses-sha-pinned and used by the release flow
gh
# every repo-tooling script derives the repo root via `git rev-parse`
git
# the hook's own runtime dependency; manifest.bats parses JSON with it
jq
# the task runner the .justfile and README document
just
# invoked by .ci/check-links
lychee
# invoked by .ci/run-lint-checks
markdownlint-cli2
# asserted by .ci/check-devshell-provides
nix
# invoked by .ci/run-lint-checks; the binary name, not its `renovate` package
renovate-config-validator
# the lint gate for the repo's entire payload
shellcheck
# the format gate; treefmt drives it, check-scripts verifies it
shfmt
# invoked by .ci/run-lint-checks
typos
# invoked by .ci/run-lint-checks
yamllint
# invoked by .ci/check-issue-forms
yq

# The baseline userland the gates shell out to. stdenv puts these on PATH
# anyway, at byte-identical store paths, so naming them buys no new binary --
# it converts an inherited nixpkgs internal (stdenv.initialPath, which no gate
# asserts and a flake.lock bump could change) into a declared dependency, and
# it is what justifies coreutils, findutils and gnugrep to the reverse pass.
# invoked by .ci/check-err-trap-hygiene and .ci/check-versions-in-sync
grep
# tests/repeat.bats walks the state dir with it
find
# bench/run creates its sample directories with it
mkdir
